.TH OTPME-GROUP 1 "2025-12-29" "OTPme 0.3.0a120" "OTPme Manual"
.SH NAME
otpme-group \- manage OTPme groups
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpme-group
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIgroup\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otpme-group
manages POSIX/LDAP groups in the OTPme system. Groups have a GID number and can contain users, tokens, and roles. Each user has a default group, and groups are exposed via LDAP with standard attributes.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Group Management
.TP
.B add \fR[\fB\-\-attributes\fR \fIattr1=val1,attr2=val2\fR] \fIgroup\fR
Create a new group, optionally with LDIF attributes.
.TP
.B del \fIgroup\fR
Delete a group.
.TP
.B show \fR[\fIgroup\fR]
Display group information. Without arguments, shows all groups.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIregex\fR]
List groups, optionally filtered by regex pattern.
.TP
.B enable \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIgroup\fR
Enable a disabled group.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Do not persist new share mounts on hosts.
.RE
.TP
.B disable \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIgroup\fR
Disable a group without deleting it.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Keep persisted share mounts on hosts (transient unmount only).
.RE
.TP
.B rename \fIgroup\fR \fInew_name\fR
Rename a group.
.TP
.B move \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-acls\fR] \fIgroup\fR \fIunit\fR
Move group to a different unit.
.TP
.B touch \fIgroup\fR
Re-index the object to fix potential index problems.
.SS Token and Role Assignment
.TP
.B add_token \fR[\fB\-\-no\-auto\-sign\fR] [\fB\-\-sign\fR \fB\-\-tags\fR \fItag1,tag2\fR] \fIgroup\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Add a token to the group.
.TP
.B remove_token \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-sign\fR] \fIgroup\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Remove a token from the group.
.TP
.B list_tokens \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIgroup\fR
List tokens assigned to the group.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR) and \fB\-\-token\-types\fR to limit the listing to the given token types.
.TP
.B add_role \fIgroup\fR \fIrole\fR
Add a role to the group.
.TP
.B remove_role \fIgroup\fR \fIrole\fR
Remove a role from the group.
.TP
.B list_roles \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIgroup\fR
List roles assigned to the group.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS User Management
.TP
.B list_users \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIgroup\fR
List users in the group.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.TP
.B list_default_group_users \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIgroup\fR
List users that have this group as their default group.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS Host Management
.TP
.B add_host \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIgroup\fR \fIhost\fR
Add a host to the group.
The host is looked for in the site of the group, or written as \fIsite\fB/\fIhost\fR to take one from another site of the realm.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on new share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Do not persist new share mounts on hosts.
.RE
.TP
.B remove_host \fR[\fB\-\-share\-notify\fR|\fB\-\-no\-share\-notify\fR] \fR[\fB\-\-no\-persist\-mount\fR] \fIgroup\fR \fIhost\fR
Remove a host from the group.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-share\-notify
Send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-share\-notify
Do not send notification to all online hosts on revoked share permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist\-mount
Keep persisted share mounts on hosts (transient unmount only).
.RE
.TP
.B list_hosts \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIgroup\fR
List hosts in the group.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS Sync User Management
.TP
.B add_sync_user \fIgroup\fR \fIuser\fR
Add a sync user to the group.
.TP
.B remove_sync_user \fIgroup\fR \fIuser\fR
Remove a sync user from the group.
.TP
.B list_sync_users \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIgroup\fR
List sync users in the group.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS Object Changelog
Every change to the object writes an entry: who made it, when, and what was done.
A change can carry a comment of its own, through the global option \fB\-\-changelog\fR.
.PP
An \fIentry_id\fR is the number the listing shows in front of an entry, counted from 0.
.PP
Only the comment of an entry can be changed or removed.
What was done and by whom stays as it is.
.PP
A command that changes something asks first; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B changelog \fIgroup\fR
Show the changelog of the group.
Needs the ACL \fBview:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B edit_changelog \fIgroup\fR \fIentry_id\fR \fIcomment\fR
Set the comment of that entry, or replace the one it has.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B del_changelog \fIgroup\fR \fIentry_id\fR
Remove the comment of that entry.
The entry itself stays, and an entry without a comment is refused.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B clear_changelog \fIgroup\fR
Remove every entry of the changelog.
.br
This needs more than the ACL \fBclear:changelog\fR: the config parameter
.B allow_changelog_clearing
has to allow it (see \fBotpme\fR(7)).
It is true by default, but where no value is found at all, clearing is refused.
OTPme asks the token you are signed in with first, then the object.
.SS Policy Management
A \fIpolicy\fR is the name of a policy, not a path.
It is looked for in the site of the group.
Which policies there are, and what each of them does, is in
.BR otpme\-policy (1).
.PP
Attaching and detaching ask before they change anything; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B add_policy \fIgroup\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Attach a policy to the group.
.br
A policy has a list of object types it is for; one that does not name \fBgroup\fR is refused.
So is a second policy of a type that allows only one per object.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBassign:policy\fR.
.TP
.B remove_policy \fIgroup\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Remove a policy from the group.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBremove:policy\fR, and that one verbatim: a plain \fBremove\fR does not cover it.
Detaching a policy takes away what it enforces, so it must not be cheaper than attaching one.
.TP
.B list_policies \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIgroup\fR
List the policies attached to the group.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
Use \fB\-\-policy\-types\fR to list only policies of the given types; these are policy types, not policy names.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBview:policies\fR.
.SS ACL Management
.TP
.B add_acl \fIgroup\fR \fIowner_type\fR \fIowner\fR \fIacl\fR
Add an access control entry.
.TP
.B del_acl \fIgroup\fR \fIacl\fR
Remove an access control entry.
.TP
.B list_acls \fIgroup\fR
Display all ACLs for the group.
.TP
.B enable_acl_inheritance \fIgroup\fR
Enable ACL inheritance from parent objects.
.TP
.B disable_acl_inheritance \fIgroup\fR
Disable ACL inheritance.
.SS Configuration and Attributes
.TP
.B config \fR[\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-a\fR] \fIgroup\fR \fIparameter\fR \fR[\fIvalue\fR]
Set a configuration parameter. Use \fB\-d\fR to delete (reset to default) or \fB\-a\fR to append the value to a list-typed parameter.
.TP
.B show_config \fIgroup\fR [\fIparameter\fR]
Show all configuration parameters.
.TP
.B get_config \fIgroup\fR \fIparameter\fR
Show the value of a single configuration parameter.
.TP
.B description \fIgroup\fR \fR[\fIdescription\fR]
Set group description.
.TP
.B info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIgroup\fR \fR[\fIinfo\fR]
Set free-form info text. If \fIinfo\fR is omitted, the current info text is
opened in the editor specified by the \fBEDITOR\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B dump_info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIgroup\fR
Dump the info text to stdout.
.TP
.B add_extension \fIgroup\fR \fIextension\fR
Add an extension to the group.
.TP
.B remove_extension \fIgroup\fR \fIextension\fR
Remove an extension.
.TP
.B add_attribute \fIgroup\fR \fIattribute\fR=\fIvalue\fR
Add an LDAP attribute.
.TP
.B del_attribute \fIgroup\fR \fIattribute\fR=\fIvalue\fR
Remove an LDAP attribute.
.TP
.B add_object_class \fIgroup\fR \fIclass\fR
Add an LDAP object class.
.TP
.B del_object_class \fIgroup\fR \fIclass\fR
Remove an LDAP object class.
.TP
.B show_ldif \fIgroup\fR \fR[\fB\-a\fR \fIattribute1,attribute2\fR]
Show LDIF representation of the group. Use \fB\-a\fR to show only given attributes.
.SS Import/Export
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR] \fIgroup\fR
Export group configuration.
.TP
.B remove_orphans \fIgroup\fR
Remove orphaned object references.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Display Options
.TP
.B \-a
Show all groups (across all units).
.TP
.B \-z \fISIZE\fR
Limit output size.
.TP
.B \-\-fields \fIFIELD1,FIELD2\fR
Display only specified fields.
.TP
.B \-\-role\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of roles shown.
.TP
.B \-\-token\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of tokens shown.
.TP
.B \-\-host\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of hosts shown.
.TP
.B \-\-policy\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of policies shown.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of items shown per object.
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-by \fIFIELD\fR
Sort output by field.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Output without headers/borders.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output as CSV.
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-sep \fISEP\fR
CSV separator character.
.TP
.B \-\-attribute \fIATTR\fR
Of \fBlist\fR: match the regex against this attribute instead of the name.
.SS Token Options
.TP
.B \-\-sign
Sign the object with default tags.
.TP
.B \-\-tags \fItag1,tag2\fR
Add tags to signature.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-auto\-sign
Do not automatically sign when adding a token.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-sign
Do not remove any signature when removing a token.
.SS General Options
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-acls
Preserve ACLs when moving group.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
Password for encrypting exports.
.PP
Global options are available for all commands. See
.BR otpme (1)
for details.
.SH CONFIG PARAMETERS
Configuration parameters can be set with the \fBconfig\fR command and displayed with \fBshow_config\fR.
For a complete description of all available parameters and their applicable object types, see
.BR otpme (7).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Managing Groups
.TP
.B otpme-group add developers
Create a new group
.TP
.B otpme-group add \-\-attributes gidNumber=1001 developers
Create group with specific GID
.TP
.B otpme-group list_users developers
List users in the group
.TP
.B otpme-group list_default_group_users developers
List users with this as default group
.SS Assigning Tokens and Roles
.TP
.B otpme-group add_token developers alice/totp
Add a token to the group
.TP
.B otpme-group add_role developers DEV_ROLE
Add a role to the group
.SS LDAP
.TP
.B otpme-group show_ldif developers
Show LDIF representation
.TP
.B otpme-group show_ldif developers \-a cn,gidNumber
Show only specific LDAP attributes
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/otpme/
OTPme data directory
